about how people who smile more often

256
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:10,282
actually have more friends.

257
00:24:11,199 --> 00:24:12,284
That's unbelievable.

258
00:24:12,743 --> 00:24:14,578
I really think
it's gonna change your whole outlook

259
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:15,787
if you smile more often.

260
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:34,640
I want the Beetle.

261
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,851
- What?
- The yellow Beetle, I want it.

262
00:24:38,018 --> 00:24:40,228
I'll make you a deal.
If I get that thing started, it's mine.

263
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:43,148
That's no deal.
That's just you taking my car.

264
00:24:43,231 --> 00:24:46,985
If I get it started, I keep it
and I work here every day for a year.

265
00:24:47,235 --> 00:24:49,321
I'll scrub the grease
off the floors, okay?

266
00:24:49,404 --> 00:24:52,282
I will pick up and organize
every scrap of paper in this place.

267
00:24:52,532 --> 00:24:55,952
I'll even detail your horrible,
disgusting toilets.

268
00:24:58,205 --> 00:25:00,165
Please. It's my birthday.

269
00:25:00,957 --> 00:25:02,292
Sorry, no deal.

270
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:05,337
'Cause we ain't hiring.

271
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:09,007
It's yours, kid. Happy birthday.

272
00:25:12,135 --> 00:25:13,136
Thank you.

273
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:17,182
Thank you, thank you, thank you!

274
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:19,434
And my toilets are gorgeous.

275
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:36,451
<i>Think about it
There must be higher love</i>

276
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:41,289
<i>Down in the heart or hidden
In the stars above</i>

277
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:46,128
<i>Without it
Life is a wasted time...</i>

278
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:50,966
Oh, God, please.

279
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:55,303
Come on.

280
00:25:59,641 --> 00:26:00,726
Oh, my...

281
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:02,310
Oh, my God!

282
00:26:03,061 --> 00:26:05,689
Oh, my God, thank you so much!
I love you!

283
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:15,699
- That thing ain't even safe to drive.
- It's a deathtrap.

284
00:26:19,786 --> 00:26:21,204
She's happy, though-

285
00:26:23,123 --> 00:26:25,625
<i>Bring me a higher love</i>

286
00:26:27,919 --> 00:26:30,046
<i>Bring me a higher love</i>

287
00:26:32,507 --> 00:26:35,218
<i>Bring me a higher love</i>

288
00:26:36,845 --> 00:26:42,392
<i>Where's that higher love
I keep thinking of?</i>

289
00:26:42,768 --> 00:26:43,852
Man.

290
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:45,812
Looks amazing.

291
00:26:58,074 --> 00:26:59,409
What?

292
00:27:56,132 --> 00:27:57,425
Oh, my God.

293
00:28:21,741 --> 00:28:23,034
Charlie, what was that noise?

294
00:28:23,118 --> 00:28:25,412
Nothing! I'm fine. Mom, you should
go back to bed. Everything's fine.

295
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:28,331
- What the hell is that?
- It's...

296
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:31,293
What is that car doing in our garage?

297
00:28:31,376 --> 00:28:32,502
Car?

298
00:28:34,504 --> 00:28:36,214
That car

299
00:28:37,424 --> 00:28:38,758
is my car.

300
00:28:39,134 --> 00:28:40,635
Uncle Hank gave it to me.

301
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:43,013
It runs. Yeah.

302
00:28:43,138 --> 00:28:44,431
Those aren't safe.

303
00:28:44,890 --> 00:28:47,225
I wish you would've told me
before you brought it home.

304
00:28:47,309 --> 00:28:48,977
Okay. Sorry.

305
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:54,024
- I'm in the middle of some stuff, Mom.
- Okay, I'll get out of your hair, but...

306
00:28:54,566 --> 00:28:57,277
Tell me things sometime.

307
00:28:57,360 --> 00:28:58,862
- I'm your mother.
- Okay.

308
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:00,572
Okay.

309
00:29:00,947 --> 00:29:01,948
Good night.

310
00:29:02,032 --> 00:29:04,910
- It really runs?
- Yeah, it really runs.

311
00:29:04,993 --> 00:29:05,994
Cool.

312
00:29:17,172 --> 00:29:18,673
You still in there?

313
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:23,595
Okay.

314
00:29:23,845 --> 00:29:25,680
A little jumpy. I'm sorry.

315
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:37,192
Okay.

316
00:30:02,801 --> 00:30:03,802
Hi.

317
00:30:16,731 --> 00:30:18,358
Oh, God, are you...

318
00:30:21,236 --> 00:30:22,737
Do you speak?

319
00:30:35,333 --> 00:30:36,668
I won't hurt you.

320
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:04,320
Can you understand me?

321
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:11,161
What are you?

322
00:31:12,954 --> 00:31:14,539
Where did you come from?

323
00:31:15,790 --> 00:31:17,333
Okay. It's okay.

324
00:31:26,509 --> 00:31:27,886
You like my shirt?

325
00:31:28,762 --> 00:31:30,055
You a metal fan?

326
00:31:30,847 --> 00:31:31,931
No, wait...

327
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:34,517
Oh, who? Me?

328
00:31:35,602 --> 00:31:36,811
Who am I?

329
00:31:38,688 --> 00:31:39,814
I'm...

330
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:42,442
Charlie.

331
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:44,944
Charlie Watson.

332
00:31:45,111 --> 00:31:46,946
I'm 18.

333
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:48,865
Today.

334
00:31:49,199 --> 00:31:51,159
Actually, it's my birthday today.

335
00:31:53,286 --> 00:31:54,454
What's your name?

336
00:31:57,957 --> 00:32:00,293
You don't know
or you don't have a name?

337
00:32:05,298 --> 00:32:07,342
You sound like a little bumblebee.

338
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:12,388
I'm gonna call you that from now on.

339
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:16,434
Bumblebee.

340
00:32:18,478 --> 00:32:20,021
Matches your outfit, too.

341
00:32:46,673 --> 00:32:48,174
I want a divorce, Roy!

342
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:50,468
Come on, Amber.
Give me one good reason.

343
00:32:50,552 --> 00:32:52,387
You tried to sleep with my sister!

344
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:53,888
Unsuccessfully!

345
00:32:53,972 --> 00:32:56,391
Yeah, you're unsuccessful at everything.

346
00:32:56,558 --> 00:32:59,060
That down payment was for a house.
You bought a car.

347
00:32:59,144 --> 00:33:02,647
How stupid are you, Roy?
We don't need a car. God!

348
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:06,067
Now, just settle down for one second
and hear me out.

349
00:33:08,111 --> 00:33:10,738
- What the hell is that?
- What?

350
00:33:13,867 --> 00:33:16,661
Oh, God, Roy,
that thing is coming right for us!

351
00:33:16,744 --> 00:33:18,413
No, no, no, no, no...

352
00:33:18,496 --> 00:33:20,415
Not my car. Not my car.

353
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:22,667
Please, God, no, not my car!

354
00:33:33,636 --> 00:33:35,638
Oh, thank God, my car.

355
00:33:36,389 --> 00:33:37,724
Yeah, I'm okay.

356
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:41,019
That's good, baby. That's good.

357
00:33:42,145 --> 00:33:43,771
Run. Run!

358
00:33:59,287 --> 00:34:00,538
God!

359
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:04,542
Is that my car?

360
00:34:07,503 --> 00:34:08,588
Hello...

361
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:24,103
Jeez!

362
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:25,521
Earth.

363
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:26,689
Roy!

364
00:34:27,523 --> 00:34:29,192
How underwhelming.

365
00:34:29,275 --> 00:34:32,445
The indigenous life is even more primitive
than I expected.

366
00:34:34,197 --> 00:34:35,198
Hey...

367
00:34:39,118 --> 00:34:40,787
I like the way they pop.

368
00:34:40,870 --> 00:34:42,247
Focus, comrade.

369
00:34:42,622 --> 00:34:47,543
B-127's distress signal came
from the western coast of this continent.

370
00:34:47,877 --> 00:34:50,546
For now, we head west.

371
00:35:04,936 --> 00:35:07,105
When do they start
letting you use nunchucks?

372
00:35:07,188 --> 00:35:08,690
I don't know, but I hope soon.

373
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:11,276
- Morning! See you guys later.
- Where you off to so fast?

374
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:14,362
Nowhere. Have a nice day.

375
00:35:16,572 --> 00:35:17,865
Morning...

376
00:35:20,326 --> 00:35:21,452
Bee?

377
00:35:24,289 --> 00:35:25,790
Bee, where are you?

378
00:35:28,876 --> 00:35:31,004
Oh, God. Oh, God.
Oh, God. Oh, God.

379
00:35:31,087 --> 00:35:32,088
Bee!

380
00:35:32,171 --> 00:35:33,756
Where did you go?

381
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:40,513
Otis!

382
00:35:41,681 --> 00:35:43,182
Have you seen my car?

383
00:35:43,266 --> 00:35:44,434
Unfortunately, yes.

384
00:35:44,517 --> 00:35:48,688
No, have you seen my car today?
It was in the garage. Someone stole it!

385
00:35:48,771 --> 00:35:50,523
No, idiot. Mom took it.

386
00:35:50,606 --> 00:35:52,108
She had to bring Conan to the vet

387
00:35:52,191 --> 00:35:53,985
because he swallowed, like,
a rubber glove or something

388
00:35:54,068 --> 00:35:55,737
and Ron needed the station wagon.

389
00:35:55,903 --> 00:35:57,196
Thank God.

390
00:35:59,866 --> 00:36:01,034
Wait.

391
00:36:06,789 --> 00:36:08,791
Hi. Excuse me. It's me again.

392
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:10,960
- We never officially met, but...
- I can't right now. Sorry.

393
00:36:11,044 --> 00:36:12,295
Nope. Yep.

394
00:36:12,628 --> 00:36:13,921
Okay.

395
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:19,635
I know, buddy. Hang in there.

396
00:36:22,221 --> 00:36:24,140
You can't eat everything you see.

397
00:36:24,474 --> 00:36:27,393
Just let this be
a good life lesson for you.

398
00:36:29,479 --> 00:36:32,231
Oh, my God. Stop it! Don't do that!

399
00:36:36,819 --> 00:36:37,820
Bee,no!

400
00:36:43,534 --> 00:36:44,535
Mom?

401
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:47,914
Jesus! Charlie, what are you doing?

402
00:36:47,997 --> 00:36:49,332
Mom, you gotta pull over.

403
00:36:49,415 --> 00:36:52,293
- What the hell is going on?
- Just pull the car over.

404
00:36:52,377 --> 00:36:55,046
Okay, okay. All right.

405
00:36:57,673 --> 00:37:01,677
Would you put that robot junk away?
What are you thinking?

406
00:37:01,969 --> 00:37:04,764
You almost gave me a heart attack.
I thought I was being carjacked.

407
00:37:04,847 --> 00:37:06,599
I'm taking the dog to the vet.

408
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:10,603
I can't believe you would take him
without me. Mom, I'm so worried about him!

409
00:37:10,686 --> 00:37:12,313
He's my dog, too, you know.

410
00:37:12,397 --> 00:37:14,941
What happened to Conan being Otis's dog?

411
00:37:15,149 --> 00:37:16,943
Mom, you're being hysterical, okay?

412
00:37:17,026 --> 00:37:19,070
You should not be driving
in such an emotional state.

413
00:37:19,153 --> 00:37:20,947
I know how you get during emergencies.

414
00:37:21,781 --> 00:37:22,949
I'm a nurse.

415
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:26,119
Not of animals.

416
00:37:31,582 --> 00:37:33,835
Okay. I'm happy for you to drive.

417
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:36,087
You weren't wearing your helmet,
by the way.

418
00:37:36,170 --> 00:37:37,630
- I saw that.
- Oh, shoot.

419
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:42,135
Keep it together, Bee.

420
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:50,810
Sir?

421
00:37:52,061 --> 00:37:53,062
Sir.

422
00:37:53,312 --> 00:37:55,565
I thought
you'd want to see this immediately.

423
00:38:00,736 --> 00:38:02,321
- They sure?
- Yes, sir.

424
00:38:02,572 --> 00:38:04,240
Two of them just made contact in Texas.

425
00:38:04,740 --> 00:38:06,576
Intel says they're heading west fast.

426
00:38:06,784 --> 00:38:08,286
Saddle up, Simmons.

427
00:38:09,328 --> 00:38:10,788
We're going to Texas.

428
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:15,501
Okay, Bee,
we need to go over a few things.

429
00:38:21,632 --> 00:38:23,217
Okay. We're all clear.

430
00:38:26,095 --> 00:38:28,848
All right. I'm re-thinking the beach.

431
00:38:31,476 --> 00:38:32,935
I'm good.

432
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:34,979
No, I'm good, thanks.

433
00:38:37,315 --> 00:38:40,902
People can be terrible about things
they don't understand.

434
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:43,696
If they find you, they'll probably
look you up in a lab somewhere

435
00:38:43,779 --> 00:38:45,156
and cut you into tiny little pieces.

436
00:38:45,406 --> 00:38:48,242
It'll be bad, trust me.

437
00:38:51,871 --> 00:38:55,541
The only person you can show
yourself around is me, okay?

438
00:38:57,877 --> 00:38:59,670
So let's practice. You ready?

439
00:39:00,129 --> 00:39:01,964
If you see anyone besides me,
what do you do?

440
00:39:05,301 --> 00:39:07,470
Great. Perfect. Come back now.

441
00:39:09,805 --> 00:39:12,475
Okay, so let's say we're driving
and all of a sudden...

442
00:39:12,642 --> 00:39:15,061
Oh, shoot! Somebody's here!
Hide, Bee, hide!

443
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:28,908
You serious?

444
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:35,248
Bee, it's too late. You're already dead.

445
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:40,670
It's all right.

446
00:39:40,836 --> 00:39:43,923
That's why we're practicing.
You'll get it.

447
00:39:44,757 --> 00:39:48,261
<i>Fox-2 on approach.
Non-biologicals are inbound.</i>

448
00:40:05,194 --> 00:40:08,698
The goal, sir,
should be to communicate with them.

449
00:40:09,031 --> 00:40:11,784
First contact with an alien species.

450
00:40:12,535 --> 00:40:15,371
I've spent my whole life
waiting for this moment.

451
00:40:15,621 --> 00:40:18,624
If they make one wrong move,
we put 'em down.

452
00:40:34,056 --> 00:40:37,226
The humans are multiplying.
Please let me kill them.

453
00:40:37,393 --> 00:40:40,896
Not yet. B-127's signal has gone silent.

454
00:40:42,064 --> 00:40:43,733
I have an idea.

455
00:40:45,234 --> 00:40:48,529
Listen up! I'm Agent Burns
and this is Dr. Powell.

456
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:52,366
We currently have 100 guns
pointed right at your head!

457
00:40:52,617 --> 00:40:54,035
So state your business.

458
00:40:54,493 --> 00:40:56,245
People of Earth,

459
00:40:56,579 --> 00:41:00,333
we are Decepticon peacekeepers
patrolling the galaxy.

460
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:01,917
What are you doing?

461
00:41:02,501 --> 00:41:04,086
This is humiliating.

462
00:41:04,587 --> 00:41:07,673
We believe a dangerous criminal
from our world

463
00:41:07,757 --> 00:41:10,843
is hiding somewhere on yours.

464
00:41:10,926 --> 00:41:12,511
How is it you think we can help?

465
00:41:14,180 --> 00:41:16,432
We need your eyes.

466
00:41:17,266 --> 00:41:18,351
Wait.

467
00:41:18,684 --> 00:41:20,811
You want access to our satellites?

468
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:23,272
Our scanners' range is limited.

469
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:26,692
Your infrastructure is primitive.

470
00:41:27,026 --> 00:41:30,529
But combined,
they could be quite powerful.

471
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:32,239
No way! Out of the question!

472
00:41:32,406 --> 00:41:35,201
We have a common enemy, Agent Burns.

473
00:41:35,368 --> 00:41:37,703
There's a war raging on our planet.

474
00:41:37,787 --> 00:41:42,458
If B-127 isn't found,
that war may find its way here.

475
00:41:42,541 --> 00:41:43,876
Perhaps...

476
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:47,213
We can find a way to help one another.

477
00:41:47,963 --> 00:41:52,635
We'll talk it over with our superiors.
In the meantime, if you could follow us.

478
00:41:52,885 --> 00:41:55,262
Very well, friend Powell.

479
00:41:55,471 --> 00:41:57,264
Take us to your leader.

480
00:42:08,067 --> 00:42:10,820
Must suck being cooped up
in a VW all day, huh?

481
00:42:12,488 --> 00:42:14,824
Is there anyone that can help you?

482
00:42:14,907 --> 00:42:16,367
Do you have a family?

483
00:42:16,450 --> 00:42:20,830
You know, like a mom, dad, siblings?
You all love each other?

484
00:42:23,499 --> 00:42:24,792
Or drive each other crazy

485
00:42:24,875 --> 00:42:27,586
and you can't wait to get away
and start a whole new life.

486
00:42:33,926 --> 00:42:35,594
Do you want me to see if I can fix it?

487
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:39,515
I'll be gentle, I promise.

488
00:42:54,447 --> 00:42:55,906
You lay down, okay?

489
00:42:59,577 --> 00:43:00,745
Hold still.

490
00:43:03,622 --> 00:43:05,332
I think maybe there's something...

491
00:43:17,219 --> 00:43:21,682
<i>B-127, I pray this message finds you.</i>

492
00:43:22,725 --> 00:43:25,644
<i>Our war rages on.</i>

493
00:43:26,187 --> 00:43:27,521
<i>...planet Earth...</i>

494
00:43:28,731 --> 00:43:29,982
<i>...survival...</i>

495
00:43:55,174 --> 00:43:57,593
Ravage, eject!

496
00:44:15,444 --> 00:44:16,946
<i>...your mission...</i>

497
00:44:17,112 --> 00:44:18,364
<i>...soldier...</i>

498
00:44:18,531 --> 00:44:19,615
<i>I...</i>

499
00:44:24,036 --> 00:44:25,412
Are you okay?

500
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:29,834
Who was that?

501
00:44:30,292 --> 00:44:33,045
That voice said something about a war.

502
00:44:34,463 --> 00:44:35,965
Do you remember anything?

503
00:44:39,635 --> 00:44:43,472
Is the VW Beetle some kind of disguise?

504
00:44:45,057 --> 00:44:46,725
Are you hiding from something?

505
00:44:49,979 --> 00:44:51,188
Are you scared?

506
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:05,119
It's broken.

507
00:45:07,371 --> 00:45:08,414
It's okay.

508
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:10,416
I think I can help.

509
00:45:12,334 --> 00:45:13,627
Let's go home.

510
00:45:18,757 --> 00:45:20,050
<i>...and a basket case,</i>

511
00:45:20,593 --> 00:45:22,261
a <i>princess...</i>

512
00:45:22,344 --> 00:45:23,596
- And a criminal.
- All right, I'm almost done.

513
00:45:24,054 --> 00:45:25,472
<i>Does that answer your question?</i>

514
00:45:26,265 --> 00:45:28,475
No way. Are you actually watching it?

515
00:45:28,559 --> 00:45:30,227
<i>Don't you forget about me</i>

516
00:45:31,228 --> 00:45:32,730
<i>Don't, don't, don't...</i>

517
00:45:32,813 --> 00:45:34,648
You can pop in another one if you want.

518
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:46,327
